<p>Use this menu to provide functions related to controls specific to the 
 driver.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="spool" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in EMF Format</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to set the spooling format to EMF. This will reduce 
 the time the printer takes to release itself from the printing process. 
 Changing the spooling format might also resolve print problems.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Depending on the application you are using, this 
 function might be disabled even if you select the EMF spool check box.</p></li>
<li><p>If this function is disabled, the following functions 
 are not available:<span class="Term-Soft"><br/>
 Layout:</span> - <span class="Term-Soft">Page Order:</span><span class="Term-Soft"><br/>
 Booklet:</span><span class="Term-Soft"><br/>
 Reverse Order Printing</span><span class="Term-Soft"><br/>
 Watermarks:</span></p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="jobload" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Job Load Distribution:</span></p>
<p>This allows you to assign the load share of the print process between 
 the printer and printer driver (computer).</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Shift Load to Driver</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Maximizes the load share of the print process on 
 the printer driver. Select this if the print process takes time and the 
 computer has a high capacity to process the job.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Shift Load to Printer</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Maximizes the load share of the print process on 
 the printer. Select this if the print process takes time and the computer 
 has a low capacity to process the job.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="emulation" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Last Emulation</span></p>
<p>Returns to the setting before the print job.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="near" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Near Standard Size</span></p>
<p>When a document is scanned for printing, its size might be detected 
 as larger than the original and a printer error might occur.</p>
<p>Select the check box to prevent this problem.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="appzoom" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Use Application Zoom</span></p>
<p>Use the application's zoom.</p>
<p>Select the check box when lines are not printed in Microsoft® or Excel® 
 files.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="dmcolor" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Always apply COLOR to dmColor setting 
 for appLication</span></p>
<p>When you perform black-and-white printing for color documents created 
 by using Microsoft® PowerPoint® and so on, some objects are filled with 
 black when printed.<br/>
If this is the case, enable this function. You will obtain print results 
 you require.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="preview" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Display Preview and Print Screen</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to display the preview screen to check print previews. 
 You can also change some of the settings on the screen.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function may not be available in a "Point 
 and Print" environment.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="reduce" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Auto Reduce:</span></p>
<p>Documents larger than the specified size can be automatically reduced 
 and printed.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For example, if you select<span class="Term-Soft"> 
 A3 (297 x 420 mm)</span>, an A2 size document will automatically be reduced 
 to A3 and printed.<br/>
 If you select <span class="Term-Soft">A4 (210 x 297 mm)</span>, a document 
 larger than A4 will automatically be reduced to A4 and printed.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="profile" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile:</span></p>
<p>Add, edit or delete a color profile in the list. You can add the new 
 color profile provided by the developer to the list and use it.</p>
